although many mcu characters show up  more than once not every hero and  villain gets a comeback despite what the  actors involved might want but that  doesn't stop them from dreaming these  are the actors who desperately want to  return to the mcu  the second season of netflix's daredevil  introduced one of the vigilante hero's  greatest supporting characters elektra  played by elodie young she next appeared  in the defenders serving as an  antagonist to daredevil and his  reluctant teammates luke cage iron fist  and jessica jones while elektra's latter  appearance ended in her apparent demise  anyone familiar with the character will  know that death rarely puts an end to  her adventures at the wizard world  virtual experiences 2020's marvel actors  panel young expressed enthusiasm at the  prospect of reprising her role she said  let me tell you i love this character  because she's so complex and broken  she's got a lot of villain in her and  also a lot of good young also shared how  much she liked working without knowing  where her character arc would end up  marvel television and my experience are  very secretive so from the moment you  start auditioning until the end of a  series you never know where it's going  sadly young couldn't say for certain  whether daredevil's former flame would  formally debut in the mcu anytime soon  before the deal between sony and marvel  made it possible for spider-man to  become iron man's protege there was  harley keener keener was the promising  young inventor who helped tony stark get  through his struggles with trauma during  the events of iron man 3. i'm cold  i can tell  you know how i can tell  because we're connected  however it took six years for the  character to make another appearance in  the mcu and a rather unexpected one at  that he showed up at tony's funeral in  avengers endgame surprising many  audiences who didn't immediately  recognize the teenaged keener in an  interview with ign simpkins mentioned  how thrilled he was at the prospect of  reprising his role he said when they  gave me the call that i was going to do  it i was freaking out and screaming in  the car simpkins also explained that at  the time his return wasn't set in stone  yet so he refrained from telling anyone  about it for fear of things going  sideways of course tony stark's heroic  sacrifice left a huge hole in the mcu  one that simpkins is more than willing  to fill when asked about the possibility  of keener donning one of tony's suits  and continuing iron man's legacy  simpkins exclaimed that he was 100  on board interestingly the time  traveling young avenger iron lad was  also mentioned as an option one that  simkin said he would do without a doubt  you'd be forgiven for thinking that  sterling k brown's participation in the  mcu was a one-and-done deal after all  his role in black panther was a brief  one regardless of its significance to  the plot brown played the role of prince  and njobu the father of eric killmonger  and uncle of t'challa in his desire to  extend aid to marginalized people  outside of the african nation of wakanda  unjobu works with ulysses claw to  smuggle out its most precious resource  the unique metal called vibranium  jobu is then killed after making an  attempt on zuri's life as such barring  any further flashback sequences in  future black panther movies it seems  unlikely that njobu will ever return  however brown isn't averse to the idea  of reprising his role in the mcu when  fans asked about the chances of him  showing up in a future marvel movie the  actor tweeted that he's open to  returning as in jobu saying if there's a  way i would be honored hashtag wakanda  forever  in the mcu josh brolin lent his acting  skills and imposing frame to the  intergalactic tyrant thanos by bringing  the character to life across multiple  films roland cemented his place in mcu  history as one of its most significant  players however brolin played another  fan favorite marvel character outside  the mcu the time traveling mutant called  cable in deadpool 2. since it's a 20th  century fox film deadpool 2 initially  existed outside the boundaries of  marvel's mainstream mcu continuity  thanks to disney's acquisition of fox  and the mcu's ongoing exploration of the  multiverse however it now appears that  pretty much anything can happen and if  comics creator rob liefeld is to be  believed brolin would be delighted to  get another shot at portraying the  mutant gunslinger comicbook.com quoted  lifefeld as saying that brolin was  itching to be cable again saying he told  me he understands how beloved his role  as thanos is but he doesn't look  completely like josh brolin meanwhile  brolin himself has revealed in  interviews that cable's appearance in  deadpool 2 was only supposed to be the  start of the character's journey brolin  told ace universe i don't know what what  you know marvel has in store  but it turned out to be one really fun  movie for me  the mcu's version of the red guardian  turned out to be significantly different  from his mainstream comic book  counterpart but david harper who brought  the character to life in 2021's black  widow didn't seem to mind in fact as he  later told insider he considers the role  to be one of the biggest gigs of his  life and he's certainly willing to  reprise it should marvel ask him to come  back harper simply said i'm down for  more harper even suggested two ideas for  red guardian's next on-screen adventure  in one scenario audiences could get a  glimpse of russia's own super soldier  through a number of scenes depicting the  red guardian in his prime harbor's other  idea for red guardian's return features  him going down the same road elena did  at the end of the film harper said when  he finds out that natasha was on that  cliff with hawkeye and maybe the version  of the story he hears is that hakai  pushed her off or something it's a  moment when red guardian turns back to  the guy he was he now wants vengeance  for her  one of the most shocking twists in black  widow involved an alternative take on a  classic marvel villain whereas the  taskmaster from the comics is a highly  skilled x-shield operative named tony  masters the mcu version of the acrobatic  antagonist is antonia dracov the  mind-controlled daughter of the red  room's overseer general drakov the  conclusion of the 2021 film saw drakov  being set free from her father's grip  after spending years as his  mind-controlled assassin with this new  development for the character olga  kurilenko believes that there's more  than enough story potential to earn  taskmaster a spot on the mcu's roster of  recurring stars in an interview with  slash film kurilenko shared a few ideas  about where the character could go next  she said it's always a danger to keep  away from being possessed and  concentrate on keeping her freedom but  it doesn't mean that she'll succeed at  it and there's always bad forces that  will try to capture her i would imagine  kurilenko added that she'd be more than  happy to reprise her role as she  believes that taskmaster is too valuable  and too skillful for marvel studios to  let go she expressed the same sentiment  in an esquire interview too but  clarified that it's up to marvel to  decide if she is to get another chance  in the spotlight  in past interviews crossbones actor  frank grillo hasn't been shy about  speaking his mind regarding marvel's  handling of his character in mcu films  during a 2021 appearance on the lights  camera bar stool podcast for instance  grillo shared why he was initially  hesitant to reprise his role in avengers  endgame saying and i was a little pissed  off about it because you know i signed  like a  seven  picture deal with them and it was like  oh you're gonna be part of the marvel  universe right and it didn't happen  however grillo has been equally candid  about how much he'd like to play brock  rumlow again whether on the silver  screen or on a disney plus show in an  interview with forbes he said i would  love to do a crossbones series just  because i have never seen a character be  on the screen so little and yet have  such a fan following i have a great  relationship with marvel and the guys  there but why didn't they pursue that  why isn't crossbones somewhere in the  mix grillo returned to voice crossbones  for the disney plus series what if but  by his own admission he'd be just as  eager to suit up himself as he said oh  yeah i often say when marvel calls i  pick up the phone  the connection between the netflix  marvel shows and the mcu has always been  tenuous at best with netflix's series  only occasionally referencing certain  events from the films and the mcu movies  completely ignoring the tv shows still  that hasn't stopped marvel fans from  hoping that the likes of daredevil and  jessica jones could somehow be folded  into the mcu cannon mainly because of  the masterful way in which those  characters were handled for example  vincent d'onofrio's performance as the  iconic villain kingpin made fans so  happy that calls for him to reprise his  role in the mcu never seemed to end  based on an interview with screenrant  the actor himself is just as keen on the  prospect of returning after being asked  about his rumored return in the upcoming  hawkeye series on disney plus dinafrio  said that he so badly wants to breathe  life into fisk's character again should  marvel studios ever grant him another  opportunity he continued i just have to  wait for marvel to ask me i think it's  very clear that i would and the fans  know that i would jump at the chance to  play again i just need to be asked  marvel studios and kevin feige have been  characteristically tight-lipped about  the status of the netflix marvel shows  whenever the question of reviving  netflix's hit shows crops up feige's  answers tend to be much like the one he  gave in a deadline interview when he  said i've been at marvel long enough to  never say never about anything that said  if it were up to jessica jones star  kristen ritter her character at least  would be making her mcu debut as she has  claimed that she'd absolutely just die  to play the tough-as-nails private eye  in an unquestionably canonical marvel  studios production in an interview with  screen rant ritter claimed that jessica  jones really struck a chord with female  audiences particularly those who had  survived abuse she said not only because  it was a great role and she's such a  badass but that character has really  resonated with people in a way that i  don't know who else has ritter added  that she would jump at the chance to  step into jessica's shoes again should  marvel call on her to do so luckily for  her rumors have since surfaced that  ritter might show up as jones on the  disney plus she-hulk series so fans  might just see the ill-mannered  investigator return sometime in the near  future  judging from the number of times  daredevil star charlie cox has been  asked if he will reprise his netflix  role in spider-man no way home it's  probably fair to say that fans are  hungry to see hell's kitchen's greatest  hero make his return while the actor has  been decidedly careful about the way in  which he responds to that particular  question cox hasn't ruled out any future  appearances in the mcu  in fact he has even suggested a number  of ways in which daredevil can integrate  himself into the mcu's version of new  york city in an interview with  comicbook.com cox expressed gratitude at  being able to portray matt murdock and  his alter ego for three seasons of the  eponymous netflix show moreover as a  self-admitted fan of the mcu cox offered  up some of his own ideas as to how his  character can return he said as a fan of  the marvel movies i've loved the little  stuff where they pop up here and there i  love the idea of jessica jones and matt  showing up in the background or matt as  a lawyer advising peter parker that'd be  really really cool of course given  spider-man's imminent legal troubles and  no way home it's clear enough that he's  going to need all the help he can get  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

